# This file tells GitHub ("Cite this repository") and Zenodo how to cite this code.
# Before the first release: fill in the ORCIDs (or delete those lines).
# After the arXiv posting: fill in the arXiv identifier in preferred-citation.
# After Zenodo mints a DOI: add it under "doi" (top level).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the article in preferred-citation."
type: software
title: "Dynamical Batching: code and configuration files"
abstract: >-
  Code, configuration files and analysis scripts for "Dynamical Batching:
  How Class-Cycling Training Shapes the Internal Structure of Neural
  Networks". Dynamical Batching is a sampling protocol that periodically
  emphasizes each class in the mini-batches while leaving the loss and
  the optimizer unchanged.
